//! **The rung table** (generated by hand, one `match` arm per rung): the `Rung`
//! enum, its dispatch to each marker's [`McRung`] methods, and the `Builder` /
//! `Loaded` enums the engine holds. Each rung's module is declared by a plain
//! `mod` line in `main.rs`; see the module docs of [`crate::rungs`] for what a
//! new rung adds.
//!
//! ~~Until 2026-11-05 this file was the `rung_table!` macro in `rungs.rs`.~~
//! **CHANGED 2026-11-05 (gh:#1252, #1253):** the macro is written out by
//! hand, one arm per rung, in ladder order. Adding a rung is now one variant
//! and one arm in every `match` below (the compiler names each one that is
//! missing).

#![allow(dead_code)]

